<title>NETHERLANDS: VNU shares dip on United bid for Blenheim.</title>
<headline>VNU shares dip on United bid for Blenheim.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dutch publisher NV Verenigd Bezit VNU fell almost two percent on Tuesday after British publisher United News and Media Plc bid for British trade exhibition group Blenheim Group Plc.</p>
<p>VNU owns 15 percent of Blenheim.</p>
<p>At 0740 GMT, VNU shares were at 31.00 guilders, down 0.60 guilders from the previous close after hitting a low of 30.80 earlier.</p>
</text>
